    story: Klaus Goldgaze was born in a lighthouse family, where wind, waves, and
      rescue bells taught people to move before panic. As a child, Klaus Goldgaze
      lived through a cave garden childhood, learning caution, secrecy, and suspicion
      of outsiders. As a young adult, Klaus Goldgaze worked through a camp guard,
      turning drills, fear, formation work, and orders into practical violence. They
      enter the dojo to win coin without taking orders.
